  "worked_solution": "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(5{y}^{3}-8{y}^{2}+16) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+16\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =5\\cdot (3{y}^{2})-8\\cdot (2y)+0 \\\\  & =15{y}^{2}-16y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{15{y}^{2}-16y}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(24,2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(24,2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15\\cdot {2}^{2}-16\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{28}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-2 & =\\frac{1}{28}(x-24) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{28}-\\frac{6}{7}+2 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{8}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
